==English==

===Etymology===
''[[en-]]'' + ''[[thrall]]'' ("to control another's mind, to enslave").

===Alternative forms===
* [[enthral]] ''(chiefly UK)''

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[hold]] [[spellbound]]; to [[bewitch]], [[charm]] or [[captivate]].
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To make [[subservient]]; to [[enslave]] or [[subjugate]].

====Synonyms====
* (''hold spellbound''): [[bewitch]], [[captivate]], [[charm]], hold in [[awe]], [[transfix]]
* (''make subservient''): [[enslave]], [[subjugate]]

